# Sport ITSM — line-ending and binary policy for git.
#
# Why this file exists: until now this repository had no `.gitattributes`,
# and on this Windows workstation `core.autocrlf=true` silently checks text
# files out as CRLF even though every committed blob is LF. Two concrete
# failures this caused, both recorded in
# `.claude/skills/ci-cd/references/gotchas.md`:
#   - `pnpm prettier --check` false-positives on Windows for files that are
#     perfectly clean in the git blob and on the Linux GitHub Actions runner
#     (the blob is LF, prettier compares against the CRLF working copy).
#   - A Windows edit to a `#!/bin/sh` shebang script (e.g.
#     docker/backend/docker-entrypoint.sh) can silently flip back to CRLF;
#     a Linux container then fails with
#     `exec .../docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory` because the
#     kernel reads the interpreter path as `/bin/sh\r`, not a missing file.
#
# Policy: normalize every text file to LF on checkout, on every platform.
# This does not rewrite what is already committed — every tracked text blob
# in this repository is already LF (`git ls-files --eol` shows 0 files with
# `i/crlf`), so adding this file only fixes the *working-tree* checkout; it
# does not, by itself, mark any file as modified.

# Let git auto-detect text vs binary per file and normalize whatever it
# classifies as text to LF on checkout — the general default that covers
# every extension not called out explicitly below (*.ts, *.md, *.json,
# *.yml/*.yaml, *.scss, *.html, …).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed directly by a Linux container entrypoint (see
# docker/backend/docker-entrypoint.sh, run as ENTRYPOINT by
# docker/backend/Dockerfile). A CRLF shebang there is a hard runtime failure,
# not a cosmetic diff — force LF explicitly instead of relying on
# `text=auto`'s heuristic detection.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Dockerfiles are parsed by the Docker daemon (Linux, even when the client is
# Windows Docker Desktop) and are hand-edited on this Windows workstation —
# pin LF for the same reason as *.sh. Matches `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dev`,
# etc. under docker/backend/ and docker/frontend/.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never let git attempt line-ending or diff normalization on
# these; doing so corrupts the file the moment git misclassifies it as text.
# Only apps/web/public/favicon.ico is tracked today; the rest are listed so
# the next icon/font asset this workspace adds is covered without a second
# change to this file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
